 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "Would you like to · Let's · 현재진행형으로 약속 말하기",
   "en": "Would you like to · Let's · present continuous for arrangements"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "초대할 때는 Would you like to + 동사 원형?을 씁니다. 함께 하자고 제안할 때는 Let's + 동사 원형입니다. 이미 정해진 약속은 현재진행형으로 말합니다: I'm meeting a friend tomorrow. 거절은 I'm afraid I can't ~로 정중하게 합니다.",
   "en": "Invite someone with 'Would you like to + base verb?'. Suggest doing something together with 'Let's + base verb'. Use the present continuous for arrangements that are already fixed: I'm meeting a friend tomorrow. Refuse politely with 'I'm afraid I can't …'."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "용도 / Use",
    "예문 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "초대 / invitation",
     "Would you like to see a film?"
    ],
    [
     "제안 / suggestion",
     "Let's meet at seven."
    ],
    [
     "수락 / accepting",
     "Yes, I'd love to. / Why not?"
    ],
    [
     "거절 / refusing",
     "I'm afraid I can't. I'm working."
    ],
    [
     "정해진 약속 / arrangement",
     "I'm meeting a friend tomorrow."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "Would you like to ~는 want to보다 정중합니다.",
    "en": "Would you like to is more polite than do you want to."
   },
   {
    "ko": "Let's 뒤에는 동사 원형: Let's go (✕ Let's to go).",
    "en": "After Let's use the base verb: Let's go (not Let's to go)."
   },
   {
    "ko": "약속에는 시간 표현을 함께 씁니다: I'm seeing him on Friday.",
    "en": "Arrangements usually come with a time: I'm seeing him on Friday."
   }
  ],
